	(text "Sensor 1 → PB6: Autonics PNP proximity sensor, PC817 opto input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "e23988a9-60a9-5ead-9905-27e411167aae")
	)
	(text "J10: 1 = +24 V (brown) through F7 100 mA PTC, 2 = sensor output (black), 3 = 0 V (blue).\nOutput ON (24 V): ≈ 2.3 mA through R32 10k + U7 LED → PB6 HIGH (3.3 V, emitter follower).\nOutput OFF, cable unplugged or broken: PB6 LOW (R33 10k pull-down).\nD18 1N4148W: reverse clamp across the opto LED. C19 100 nF / 50 V: supply decoupling + ESD.\nA shorted sensor cable trips F7 only: the other sensor and the board keep running."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 33.02 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "20104f9c-bb38-5a8d-99c2-aa5a403e085e")
	)
	(text "Sensor 2 → PC15: Autonics PNP proximity sensor, PC817 opto input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 78.74 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "0b7a89cc-a22e-5497-8742-2a117fa08be5")
	)
	(text "J11: 1 = +24 V (brown) through F8 100 mA PTC, 2 = sensor output (black), 3 = 0 V (blue).\nOutput ON (24 V): ≈ 2.3 mA through R34 10k + U8 LED → PC15 HIGH (3.3 V, emitter follower).\nOutput OFF, cable unplugged or broken: PC15 LOW (R35 10k pull-down).\nD19 1N4148W: reverse clamp across the opto LED. C20 100 nF / 50 V: supply decoupling + ESD.\nA shorted sensor cable trips F8 only: the other sensor and the board keep running."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 88.9 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "becbe43e-15f5-53af-b988-6ab2d5adca82")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 15.24 132.08)
		(end 297.18 175.26)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "b9d407df-75c3-5008-8777-c51e1da601f2")
	)
	(text "Sensor inputs: notes"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 134.62 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "5799d55d-6664-5c94-9edb-d9d6aceb5c72")
	)
	(text "For 3-wire PNP (sourcing) 24 V sensors, e.g. Autonics PRD08 / PR series (brown +V, black OUT, blue 0 V).\nNPN (sinking) sensors need a different input circuit.\n\nSame circuit as the MES4-Flasher sensor channels 3 / 4 (PB6 / PC15), without the INA226 supply monitors.\nGPIO budget: all 14 module pins are used (Main sheet). More sensors can use the TCA9535 expander\n(Relays 3-4 sheet), which has 12 spare inputs (P04-P17), polled over I²C.\n\nPB6: the ST bootloader enables a 25-55 kΩ pull-up on PB6 (blank chip only); with the 10k pull-down it\nreads LOW, which is harmless for an input. PC15: input only (RTC-domain pin, CIF rule 10): fine here.\nInterrupts: PB6 → EXTI6. PC15 shares EXTI15 with PA15 (INA226 ALERT): give EXTI15 to PC15 (sensor 2)\nand poll ALERT, which the INA226 latches (MASK/ENABLE LEN = 1), so no fault is missed.\nNo back-powering: the PC817 collectors run from +3V3_MOD (module finger 4), so nothing drives the\nmodule pins while it is unpowered."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 139.7 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "43909cc9-57bd-5fc0-b8d4-8d47283b4ace")
	)
